girl, but I had her dealt with.

256
00:13:53,360 --> 00:13:54,831
I hope that means killed.

257
00:13:54,980 --> 00:13:58,020
No, I didn't kill her, she's just a kid.

258
00:13:58,720 --> 00:14:02,477
You there, go into town,
find this girl and kill her.

259
00:14:02,560 --> 00:14:05,177
But, sir, you can't be serious.

260
00:14:05,260 --> 00:14:07,057
She's just a little girl, sir.

261
00:14:07,140 --> 00:14:09,017
I don't care if she's a child or not.

262
00:14:09,100 --> 00:14:11,700
Anyone who disobeys my
orders is a traitor.

263
00:14:12,880 --> 00:14:14,780
No, sir, I can't do it.

264
00:14:19,680 --> 00:14:20,510
Lieutenant!

265
00:14:21,580 --> 00:14:23,300
You, you killed him!

266
00:14:23,720 --> 00:14:27,640
My strength was what I used
to rise to the rank of captain

267
00:14:28,580 --> 00:14:31,900
Listen, in this world,
titles are what matter.

268
00:14:32,580 --> 00:14:36,577
That means by being the captain of this
base and the highest ranking officer,

269
00:14:36,660 --> 00:14:40,300
I am the most superior person
as far as the eye can see.

270
00:14:41,280 --> 00:14:44,720
This means that I do everything right.

271
00:14:45,960 --> 00:14:47,640
Am I correct, men?

272
00:14:47,900 --> 00:14:49,680
Sir, you are correct, sir!

273
00:14:49,860 --> 00:14:52,389
Let's put killing the
girl on hold for now.

274
00:14:52,920 --> 00:14:56,277
Observe, the greatest symbol
of my unending authority.

275
00:14:56,360 --> 00:14:59,780
It took years to complete, but here it is.

276
00:15:00,100 --> 00:15:01,420
Now stand it up!

277
00:15:02,400 --> 00:15:06,440
Display my greatness at the top
of this base for all to see!

278
00:15:09,500 --> 00:15:10,500
That's weird.

279
00:15:10,740 --> 00:15:11,916
There's nobody here.

280
00:15:12,280 --> 00:15:16,398
I gotta find that crazy idiot's son
and get Zoro's sword back for him.

281
00:15:17,540 --> 00:15:18,820
Pullman, harder!

282
00:15:24,080 --> 00:15:25,140
You there.

283
00:15:28,620 --> 00:15:30,360
You bumped it.

284
00:15:31,360 --> 00:15:33,831
Sounds like something's going on up there.

285
00:15:34,900 --> 00:15:38,080
I'm sorry, sir. I was
reckless. I didn't mean it.

286
00:15:38,220 --> 00:15:40,632
I consider the slightest scratch on this.

287
00:15:40,840 --> 00:15:46,000
Nothing less than a traitorous
activity that's punishable by death.

288
00:15:46,580 --> 00:15:48,227
Guess I should check it out.

289
00:15:50,060 --> 00:15:52,297
Jump, jump, rocket!

290
00:15:52,380 --> 00:15:53,400
You're perfect!

291
00:15:55,260 --> 00:15:56,800
I took too far!

292
00:15:57,440 --> 00:15:58,760
What is that thing?

293
00:15:59,040 --> 00:16:01,660
It flew up from the ground! Got it!

294
00:16:13,700 --> 00:16:14,940
Sorry about that.

295
00:16:17,820 --> 00:16:22,800
Seize him and hold him so I can kill
him myself! Sir! Right away! That's him!

296
00:16:22,920 --> 00:16:23,750
That's the guy!

297
00:16:23,833 --> 00:16:25,437
He's the one who pushed me, Daddy!

298
00:16:25,520 --> 00:16:26,461
Hey, that's you!

299
00:16:27,020 --> 00:16:29,097
I've been looking for
you all over the place!

300
00:16:29,180 --> 00:16:31,457
You have something that I
really need to get back!

301
00:16:31,540 --> 00:16:32,370
Let me go!

302
00:16:32,453 --> 00:16:33,283
Help that bow!

303
00:16:33,380 --> 00:16:35,300
Do not let that man escape!

304
00:16:35,680 --> 00:16:38,177
Captain, there's someone
in the crucifixion yard!

305
00:16:38,260 --> 00:16:39,090
What?

306
00:16:43,920 --> 00:16:47,040
I'm surrounded by traitors.

307
00:16:47,600 --> 00:16:49,577
You have to get out of here, Zoro.

308
00:16:49,660 --> 00:16:52,497
That maniac's gonna kill you
for what you're doing right now.

309
00:16:52,580 --> 00:16:56,109
I can't stand to watch the
marines behave like this anymore.

310
00:16:56,640 --> 00:16:58,640
A true marine should be honorable.

311
00:16:59,420 --> 00:17:01,057
Look, kid, I can't leave.

312
00:17:01,140 --> 00:17:02,520
I got ten days left.

313
00:17:02,700 --> 00:17:03,530
And then they're...

314
00:17:03,613 --> 00:17:04,443
Well, not quite.

315
00:17:04,526 --> 00:17:05,617
They're gonna execute you tomorrow.

316
00:17:05,700 --> 00:17:06,530
The what?

317
00:17:06,613 --> 00:17:08,977
El Meppo never intended
to honor your agreement.

318
00:17:09,060 --> 00:17:11,057
He planned on killing you from the start.

319
00:17:11,140 --> 00:17:13,120
Which made Luffy really angry.

320
00:17:13,360 --> 00:17:14,948
So we just knocked him out.

321
00:17:16,040 --> 00:17:16,897
He did?

322
00:17:16,980 --> 00:17:20,804
Now that the marines are mad,
they're dead set on catching Luffy.

323
00:17:20,900 --> 00:17:23,937
Don't worry, I'm not going to ask
you to become a pirate, though.

324
00:17:24,020 --> 00:17:25,657
But I hope you'll help them.

325
00:17:25,740 --> 00:17:28,152
You have a lot of strength you can offer.

326
00:17:31,660 --> 00:17:35,778
Luffy's the only person here who can
actually save you from execution.

327
00:17:37,000 --> 00:17:42,520
And, of course, you're the only one here
who can save him from a very similar fate.

328
00:17:44,940 --> 00:17:46,280
End of the line!

329
00:17:50,000 --> 00:17:52,097
Okay, so tell me where Zoro's sword is.

330
00:17:52,180 --> 00:17:53,457
I'll tell you, I promise.

331
00:17:53,540 --> 00:17:56,217
Just please stop dragging
me across the carpet.

332
00:17:56,300 --> 00:17:57,241
Fine, which way?

333
00:17:57,360 --> 00:17:59,240
In my room, we just passed it.

334
00:17:59,380 --> 00:18:00,577
Behind you on the left.

335
00:18:00,660 --> 00:18:02,417
Why didn't you say so earlier?

336
00:18:02,500 --> 00:18:04,277
Oh, we gotta go all the way back.

337
00:18:04,360 --> 00:18:05,190
Don't move.

338
00:18:05,273 --> 00:18:07,860
Except for letting Helmepo go. No way.

339
00:18:09,880 --> 00:18:11,998
You can try shooting me if you want.

340
00:18:12,440 --> 00:18:14,060
No, please don't shoot.

341
00:18:14,320 --> 00:18:15,737
Get the hell out of the way.

342
00:18:15,820 --> 00:18:21,700
For the crime of treason against me, I
sentence you both to die where you stand.

343
00:18:24,640 --> 00:18:26,060
This looks like yours.

344
00:18:29,720 --> 00:18:30,550
Bingo!

345
00:18:31,740 --> 00:18:33,680
Hold on, there are three here.

346
00:18:33,920 --> 00:18:36,273
Hey weirdo, which one of these is Serious?

347
00:18:36,560 --> 00:18:38,120
I see passed out.

348
00:18:40,380 --> 00:18:41,210
Kobe!

349
00:18:48,500 --> 00:18:51,637
You've been pulling some
interesting moves around here.

350
00:18:51,720 --> 00:18:52,550
What is this?

351
00:18:52,680 --> 00:18:55,220
Some kind of poorly executed coup?

352
00:18:55,540 --> 00:18:57,599
You two planned with the Straw Hat?

353
00:18:57,880 --> 00:19:00,586
I've always fought alone
like a real man does,

354
00:19:00,820 --> 00:19:05,080
not like a coward who hides behind
his wall of expendable cronies.

355
00:19:06,180 --> 00:19:09,340
Roronoa Saru, don't you
dare underestimate me.

356
00:19:09,600 --> 00:19:13,100
You may be a strong fighter,
But under my authority,

357
00:19:13,300 --> 00:19:16,660
you're just a rat we throw
out with the trash. Take aim!

358
00:19:17,380 --> 00:19:18,210
No.

359
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:23,160
I can't afford to die here.

360
00:19:27,640 --> 00:19:29,000
Match over!

361
00:19:29,380 --> 00:19:34,400
And the winner, Conney, with
2,000 total wins and zero losses.

362
00:19:35,500 --> 00:19:36,500
Damn it!

363
00:19:36,880 --> 00:19:38,120
You're weak, Zoro.

364
00:19:38,520 --> 00:19:39,860
Nothing ever changes.

365
00:19:40,360 --> 00:19:43,380
You know, for a boy, you're pathetic.

366
00:19:43,740 --> 00:19:45,460
But Zoro isn't weak at all.

367
00:19:45,660 --> 00:19:48,077
He's one of the strongest
out of all the guys.

368
00:19:48,160 --> 00:19:49,677
He's even beaten grown-ups.

369
00:19:49,760 --> 00:19:52,420
But he's nowhere as strong as me.

370
00:19:52,920 --> 00:19:55,957
Even with two swords, a
weakling is still a weakling.

371
00:19:56,040 --> 00:19:58,897
You losers would do good to
remember that and keep quiet.

372
00:19:58,980 --> 00:20:02,921
Your howling makes you look even
more pitiful than you already are.

373
00:20:10,920 --> 00:20:12,980
You've grown so strong, Zoro.

374
00:20:13,360 --> 00:20:16,654
And yet, you continue to lose
every match against Kuina.

375
00:20:17,200 --> 00:20:18,030
Sensei!

376
00:20:18,113 --> 00:20:19,937
Are you getting her special training?

377
00:20:20,020 --> 00:20:22,557
She might be her daughter,
but that's not fair!

378
00:20:22,640 --> 00:20:23,797
You shouldn't cheat!

379
00:20:23,880 --> 00:20:24,710
Calm down.

380
00:20:24,860 --> 00:20:26,625
I've done nothing of the sort.

381
00:20:27,040 --> 00:20:29,620
You see, Zoro has grown stronger.

382
00:20:30,040 --> 00:20:33,540
But Kuina has continued
to grow stronger as well.

383
00:20:34,500 --> 00:20:35,800
Zoro! Zoro?

384
00:20:36,240 --> 00:20:37,680
I'm gonna go clean up.

385
00:20:45,680 --> 00:20:46,520
Damn it!

386
00:20:46,780 --> 00:20:49,420
Why can't I beat Clan? Why? Why?

387
00:20:49,740 --> 00:20:54,520
I'm going to be the strongest swordsman
in the world, so why can't I beat her?

388
00:21:05,620 --> 00:21:08,320
Thorough, it's laid
out. What are you doing?

389
00:21:09,120 --> 00:21:11,880
Funny, I was gonna ask
you the same question.

390
00:21:12,120 --> 00:21:13,944
What are you doing out so late?

391
00:21:15,960 --> 00:21:19,340
I've come here to challenge
you to your City fight.

392
00:21:19,640 --> 00:21:23,111
And it's gonna be the last
fight you and me will ever have.

393
00:21:23,280 --> 00:21:24,440
This ends tonight.

394
00:21:24,980 --> 00:21:26,660
Fight me with a real sword.

395
00:21:27,160 --> 00:21:28,960
You do have one, don't you?

396
00:21:31,600 --> 00:21:32,460
Real swords?

397
00:21:36,880 --> 00:21:37,710
You're on.

398
00:21:58,620 --> 00:22:01,337
I'm not

399
00:22:01,420 --> 00:22:06,340
going to die.

400
00:22:14,640 --> 00:22:16,780
Win, number 2001.

401
00:22:23,840 --> 00:22:24,980
Damn it!

402
00:22:26,960 --> 00:22:28,420
I hate it!

403
00:22:33,080 --> 00:22:36,668
I'm the one who should be crying
out of frustration, not you.

404
00:22:39,220 --> 00:22:40,640
When girls grow up,

405
00:22:40,940 --> 00:22:45,058
it's natural for us to develop into
physically weaker beings than men.

406
00:22:46,160 --> 00:22:48,572
Even you will catch up to me soon enough.

407
00:22:50,040 --> 00:22:54,922
I've always heard you say to me, you're
going to be the world's greatest swordsman.

408
00:22:56,040 --> 00:23:00,400
When I told my father the same
thing, he said I could never be that.

409
00:23:01,600 --> 00:23:06,420
And I know, I know that, but
it's just so frustrating.

410
00:23:11,140 --> 00:23:13,757
You're lucky, Zoro, being born as a man.

411
00:23:13,840 --> 00:23:16,657
All I ever wanted was to be
the world's greatest swordsman.

412
00:23:16,740 --> 00:23:19,387
My breasts have even
started to grow out now.

413
00:23:19,700 --> 00:23:20,897
If only...

414
00:23:20,980 --> 00:23:23,120
if I'd just been born a man!

415
00:23:25,120 --> 00:23:28,677
Don't fly off in the mouth whining
like that after you beat me!

416
00:23:28,760 --> 00:23:30,160
Because it's not fair!

417
00:23:30,420 --> 00:23:32,797
You're my goal, you know
how this makes me feel?

418
00:23:32,880 --> 00:23:33,710
Zoro.

419
00:23:33,793 --> 00:23:34,936
Boy this, girl that,

420
00:23:35,100 --> 00:23:38,657
are you going to keep up that same
kind of talk after I beat you someday?

421
00:23:38,740 --> 00:23:40,211
Like skill is irrelevant!

422
00:23:40,640 --> 00:23:44,797
That's just an insult to all of the
training I've been pouring on every day!

423
00:23:44,880 --> 00:23:46,900
So don't say that crap, would ya?

424
00:23:49,220 --> 00:23:50,520
Now promise me!

425
00:23:51,400 --> 00:23:55,317
Promise me that someday one of us will
be the world's greatest swordsman!

426
00:23:55,400 --> 00:23:57,800
We'll compete and see who gets there!

427
00:24:01,940 --> 00:24:03,820
Dummy, you're so weak.

428
00:24:07,600 --> 00:24:08,720
It's a promise.

429
00:24:12,720 --> 00:24:16,460
Gotta get stronger so I
can hold lots of swords.

430
00:24:17,040 --> 00:24:19,160
Two's not enough, I'll use three!

431
00:24:24,380 --> 00:24:26,140
What do you guys want?

432
00:24:29,420 --> 00:24:30,250
Kuina.

433
00:24:32,060 --> 00:24:33,980
Kuina is dead, Zoro.

434
00:24:46,060 --> 00:24:49,413
They said she slipped and fell
down the storehouse steps.

435
00:24:49,960 --> 00:24:50,790
Storehouse?

436
00:24:50,900 --> 00:24:54,018
Looking for a sharpening
stone for her beloved sword.

437
00:24:54,140 --> 00:24:55,757
What would she need that for?

438
00:24:55,840 --> 00:24:56,720
I don't know.

439
00:24:57,160 --> 00:24:58,860
She was just a child, too.

440
00:24:59,220 --> 00:25:01,279
Who knows why anyone does anything?

441
00:25:01,460 --> 00:25:03,480
There's no way to rationalize it.

442
00:25:04,140 --> 00:25:08,081
Guess you never know what's waiting
for you around the next corner.

443
00:25:13,840 --> 00:25:19,320
It may appear otherwise to the blind
eye, But people are quite fragile things.

444
00:25:33,800 --> 00:25:34,680
Sensei...

445
00:25:36,500 --> 00:25:39,000
I ask that you let me have that sword.

446
00:25:41,300 --> 00:25:42,540
Kawina's sword?

447
00:25:44,160 --> 00:25:45,500
I'll get stronger!

448
00:25:45,780 --> 00:25:48,133
Stronger than she ever was, you hear me?

449
00:25:48,360 --> 00:25:51,478
Strong enough that my name
reaches up to the heavens!

450
00:25:56,160 --> 00:25:58,997
I am going to be the
world's greatest swordsman!

451
00:25:59,080 --> 00:26:00,557
I promised her!

452
00:26:00,640 --> 00:26:01,797
I promised!

453
00:26:01,880 --> 00:26:02,860
I did!

454
00:26:09,900 --> 00:26:11,460
The sword is yours.

455
00:26:16,280 --> 00:26:21,180
I leave her spirit and
her dreams in your hands.

456
00:26:46,500 --> 00:26:50,420
Gum, gum, rocket! Fire!

457
00:26:54,740 --> 00:26:57,240
What? Wolf, no! Straw Hat!

458
00:27:02,600 --> 00:27:03,740
See ya!

459
00:27:09,020 --> 00:27:10,777
That won't work on me!

460
00:27:10,860 --> 00:27:12,980
Told you I was strong! What the?

461
00:27:13,420 --> 00:27:14,940
Who the hell are you?

462
00:27:15,740 --> 00:27:17,380
My name's Monkey D.

463
00:27:17,580 --> 00:27:20,780
Luffy, and I'm gonna
be king of the pirates!

464
00:27:29,800 --> 00:27:35,940
As a kid, I never stopped
searching for a great treasure.

465
00:27:36,760 --> 00:27:40,577
I had a map in my mind.

466
00:27:40,660 --> 00:27:43,237
That I knew would lead me.

467
00:27:43,320 --> 00:27:47,417
I had to find my way to that place.

468
00:27:47,500 --> 00:27:50,357
Before someone could beat me.

469
00:27:50,440 --> 00:27:54,497
The promised land was in my grasp.

470
00:27:54,580 --> 00:27:57,160
And I wouldn't let go.

471
00:27:58,260 --> 00:28:00,937
La la la la.

472
00:28:01,020 --> 00:28:02,297
My only dream.

473
00:28:02,380 --> 00:28:04,497
La la la la la.

474
00:28:04,580 --> 00:28:10,160
I won't stop chasing
it until it comes true.

475
00:28:12,220 --> 00:28:18,797
But the world ever changes
as I call out your name.

476
00:28:18,880 --> 00:28:25,520
We return to the time when
everything's the same.

477
00:28:26,200 --> 00:28:32,600
As long as I'm with you,
my memories won't fade.

478
00:28:33,260 --> 00:28:37,777
Waiting for that one true dream?

479
00:28:37,860 --> 00:28:39,460
We'll be back.
